{
 "line": "This metal robot melts through a cage\u2026 then gets remolded into shape. It\u2019s made from gallium packed with tiny magnetic particles. A magnetic field heats it into liquid. Another magnet steers the metal. And when it cools, it hardens again. But researchers tested something even stranger. Inside a model stomach, it melted around a trapped object, hardened, and carried it back out. Would you let one inside you?",
